## Death
Once we receive written notification of death and a certified copy of the death certificate, we will confirm to the personal representative what our requirements are to allow us to take instructions from them.  Once these requirements are met, we will be able to take instructions from the personal representative and this agreement will become binding on them. We will stop ongoing service fees as soon as feasibly possible having been notified of the client's death.  Any ongoing fee that has been received up to that point can be considered to cover the work financial advisers may be requested to carry out.  If additional work is required or if ongoing fees have not been received a time-based fee may be charged.
If the account is held in joint names and we are notified that one of the account holders has died, subject to the last Will, we will continue to take instructions from the surviving account holder and transfer the account into their sole name or take instruction from the deceased's executors.
## Variation
We may amend this agreement from time to time, in whole or in part, for the following reasons:
To reflect changes in costs, charges, taxes, duties or interest that are relevant to your advisory services or that we incur or expect to incur in providing our advisory services to you.
To reflect changes in law, FCA rules or regulations, or decisions of the Financial Ombudsman Service
To meet regulatory requirements or industry guidance or best practice
To make this agreement easier to understand or fairer, or to correct mistakes.
To reflect changes in market practice or conditions
To reflect the way that our advisory services are used and ensure that the costs of those advisory services are allocated fairly among our clients.
We will give you at least 30 days' written notice of any changes to this agreement unless we are required to make the change sooner (for example for regulatory reasons).  Such notice may be delivered either by post, email or via our portal .  If you do not agree to the change, you may contact us to end the advisory services before the change takes effect and receive a refund for any advisory services paid for but not received, save that you do not have a right to end the agreement where any change is required by law or regulation.
